# Brace end plate, bolts in shear

Single shear, four bolts M20 8.8, shear plane through the threads.
Plate 10 mm S355. Brace force from the frame analysis.

```calc
V_Ed = 200 kN
n    = 4                  # bolts
F_v_Ed = V_Ed / n         # per bolt
```

## Bolt and plate data

```calc
d    = 20 mm
d_0  = 22 mm              # hole
A_s  = 245 mm^2           # tensile stress area
f_ub = 800 MPa
t    = 10 mm              # plate
f_u  = 490 MPa            # S355, t ≤ 40 mm
e_1  = 40 mm              # end distance, load direction
e_2  = 40 mm              # edge distance
p_1  = 70 mm              # pitch, load direction
gamma_M2 = 1.25
```

## Shear resistance per bolt, Table 3.4

Thread in the shear plane, class 8.8: α_v = 0.6.

```calc
alpha_v = 0.6
F_v_Rd = alpha_v f_ub A_s / gamma_M2 to kN
check F_v_Ed <= F_v_Rd
```

## Bearing resistance per bolt, Table 3.4

End bolts govern in the load direction.

```calc
alpha_d = e_1 / (3 d_0)
alpha_b = min(alpha_d, f_ub / f_u, 1.0)
k_1 = min(2.8 e_2 / d_0 - 1.7, 2.5)
F_b_Rd = k_1 alpha_b f_u d t / gamma_M2 to kN
check F_v_Ed <= F_b_Rd
```

## Group resistance, 3.7

Bearing is ductile (F_b,Rd > F_v,Rd not required here), so the group resistance is the sum of the individual bearing resistances, capped by shear.

```calc
F_Rd = n * min(F_v_Rd, F_b_Rd) to kN
check V_Ed <= F_Rd
```

## Spacing limits, Table 3.3

```calc
check e_1 >= 1.2 d_0
check e_2 >= 1.2 d_0
check p_1 >= 2.2 d_0
```

## Summary

Governing per-bolt resistance {min(F_v_Rd, F_b_Rd)} against {F_v_Ed =}; group utilization {V_Ed / F_Rd}.
